    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64037" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύγξ</span></b>  (A), ὁ, ἡ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγκός
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύγγα</span> in <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			863
		</span></i> is perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύγκα</span>
			, but cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύγγιος</span>):—<i>lynx, Felis lynx,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Hom.
				19.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαλιαὶ λύγκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					579
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				500b15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				175
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>caracal, Felis caracal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				14.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.85
			</span></i>, etc. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγγούριον</span>).
			(OHG. <i>luhs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Germ.
			</span></i>
			<i>luchs</i>, Lith. <i>lúšis.</i>)</div>
